        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Walmart sells treadmills, but check who is selling yours.</strong>
            A machine sold and shipped by Walmart comes with Walmart's long return window and
            Walmart as your contact. A Marketplace listing comes with the seller's terms, which can
            mean 30 days, a restocking fee and return freight to arrange yourself.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Judge the machine on its specification and warranty, not the price beside it, and compare
            the delivered price with
            <a href="/treadmills-for-sale/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">other places to buy</a>.
            For a mainstream model sold by Walmart at a good price, it is a sound place to buy.
          </p>
